<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    <parent>
        <groupId>org.os890.jawelte</groupId>
        <artifactId>jawelte-tests-cdi-module</artifactId>
        <version>0.3.0</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>
    <artifactId>jawelte-tests-cdi-module-scenario-61-late-synthetic-bean-not-auto-mocked</artifactId>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>
    <name>jawelte tests/cdi-module scenario 61: a synthetic bean registered late must not be competed with by an auto-mock</name>
    <description>Reproduction for \#124, generalised away from datasource-module: an extension registers a synthetic bean in AfterBeanDiscovery with a late \@Priority, so it runs after cdi-module's auto-mock re-check would have. CDI does not specify the order of AfterBeanDiscovery observers across extensions, so whether auto-mock sees such a bean is otherwise a matter of classpath luck.</description>
</project>
